From 2fbef56c8d5c4ff1dd456822cd34228132774b2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:28:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agent_ui): session time and tool usage in the turn stats

The turn stats answered one question -- how long did the last turn take --
and only past 30 seconds, so a short turn left no trace and nothing added the
turns up. This extends the same row, behind the same show_turn_stats setting:

- The turn's duration is always shown, while it runs and when it ends. The
  30-second threshold existed to keep a quick reply from flashing a counter;
  with the row now the place to read the session's pace, a missing number
  reads as "not measured" rather than "short". STOPWATCH_THRESHOLD goes with
  its last use. The token count keeps its own threshold, and no longer waits
  for the clock to appear.

- "<duration> total" sums the finished turns, plus the running one while it
  runs. It lives on the view, not on the thread: it counts agent time since
  the thread was opened in this window, says so in its tooltip, and starts
  from zero when the thread is reopened. Persisting it would mean a field in
  the thread metadata store for one number -- left for when it is asked for.

- "<n> tool calls" counts the thread's tool-call entries, and its tooltip
  breaks them down three ways: by tool; MCP calls by server, read off Claude
  Code's mcp__<server>__<tool> naming; and the programs the terminal calls
  ran. It is derived from the entries on every render of the last turn's
  row, so it is right for a reopened thread too -- as far as the replayed
  history reaches, which after a compaction is the summary onward.

The tool name is ACP's own ToolCall.name, which this adapter sets on every
tool call; an agent that sends none is counted by ToolKind instead.

Programs come from the Execute calls' raw_input.command through a small
scanner, not a shell parser: it splits on unquoted ;, |, && and ||, and on
newlines; it skips heredoc bodies, so a python3 - <<'EOF' script is one
python3 and not one program per line; it drops environment assignments,
paths and comments; and it leaves out cd, export, set, unset, source and ".",
which change the shell rather than run anything and would otherwise top
every list. A program behind a wrapper (sudo make, xargs grep) counts as the
wrapper. The scanner and the MCP naming carry unit tests.

The row these join is the one 0026 moved to the left, clear of the floating
controls; the items are joined by the row's existing separator dot.

Pure Zed and generic ACP -- nothing needs the adapter -- so it rides the
claude-agent-acp-plus flag BY CHOICE, like 0010, 0012, 0014 and 0026.

(0.2.3_p20261009): the grouping is `ToolUsage::from_calls`, tested for unnamed calls, MCP
servers and programs read only from Execute calls; odd commands never panic; a
turn's time is added to the session once even if stop_turn runs twice.
---

